PROJECT CONTEXT — this project has two codelines, each a standalone TypeScript + vitest
repository:

- mocka (path: /home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-a) — single source file src/fares.ts,
  single test file test/fares.test.ts. Exports: fareFor, totalFor, Rider, BASE_FARE_CENTS,
  CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS. The bug (MOCK3-1) is a boundary condition in fareFor: the comparison
  `rider.age > 65` excludes riders aged exactly 65 from the concession fare; the fix changes
  the operator to `>=`. totalFor delegates to fareFor, so no separate change is needed there.
  Tests use vitest describe/it/expect; the existing suite does not yet assert age 65.
- mockb (path: /home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-b) — single source file src/schedule.ts,
  single test file test/schedule.test.ts. Exports: formatStops, totalMinutes, Stop. The bug
  (MOCK3-2) is an off-by-one in formatStops: the loop bound `i < stops.length - 1` skips the
  final stop; the fix changes the bound to `i < stops.length`. totalMinutes is unaffected.
  Tests use vitest describe/it/expect; the existing suite does not yet assert that the last
  stop appears in the formatted output.

Both codelines are ESM (`"type": "module"`), strict TypeScript, moduleResolution "bundler".
Test command in both: `vitest run`. Type-check / build command in both: `tsc --noEmit`. No lint
is configured.

The roles include one implementer (typescript-bugfix-engineer) spanning both codelines and two
investigators (mocka-investigator, mockb-investigator) each scoped to one codeline. The
investigators read and characterise the codebase but do NOT deliver source changes — their
output is analysis, not a repository edit. Only typescript-bugfix-engineer edits source files.
